      "persona": "oncall.engineer",
      "seconds": 3.51,
      "answer": "To fail over the claims Aurora cluster, you should use the `lm-dbctl` wrapper rather than calling the AWS CLI directly. Execute the following command:\n\n`lm-dbctl failover claims-aurora-prod-v2 --reason INC<number>`\n\nThis process is expected to result in under 35 seconds of write unavailability because RDS Proxy holds client connections during the switch, meaning `claims-api` does not need a restart. After the failover, you can confirm the status by running `lm-dbctl status claims-aurora-prod-v2` to ensure the writer and both readers are available. Note that the on-call engineer may perform this failover without paging the DBA team, but should inform `LM-DBA` in the incident afterward.\n\n(Failing over the claims Aurora cluster (Aurora PostgreSQL 16), reviewed 2026-08-19)",
